#
# Conformance case: teleology/currency-freshness-window.
#
# An action schema carries a logic:FreshnessGuard whose currency is an EXPLICIT
# valid-time window (logic:freshnessWindow) rather than a max-age horizon: the datum
# backing the precondition is authoritative only while a probe's logic:decisionTime
# falls inside the closed [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd]
# interval (here 2026-06-16 .. 2026-06-18). This is the second, orthogonal freshness
# axis — GMEOW's native subsumption of an openEHR decision-rule time_window (a named
# bounding interval such as "the current episode"), DISTINCT from the age horizon
# (currency-freshness-guard exercises that axis). Two gate probes share the same schema,
# state, datum, and guard but differ in decision time: probeInWindow decides at
# 2026-06-17 (inside the window → logic:GateAdmitted) and probeOffWindow decides at
# 2026-06-20 (after the window closes → logic:GateUndetermined, NOT admitted on an
# off-episode datum and NOT denied — the evaluator declines to gate outside the
# declared validity interval).
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/currency-freshness-window/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
